===South Korea vs Mexico===
The two teams had met in 12 matches, including one game at the [[1998 FIFA World Cup]] group stage, won by Mexico [[1998 FIFA World Cup Group E#South Korea vs Mexico|3–1]].<ref name=Kit14/> The match was attended by the President of South Korea, [[Moon Jae-in]].

In the 12th minute, [[Hirving Lozano]] made a block to deny [[Lee Yong (footballer, born 1986)|Lee Yong]]. Nine minutes later, [[Son Heung-min]] shot a low drive which [[Héctor Moreno]] helped to keep out. [[Jang Hyun-soo]] handled [[Andrés Guardado]]'s cross and the referee awarded a penalty, [[Carlos Vela]] stepped up and sent [[Jo Hyeon-woo]] the wrong way. Two minutes later, [[Miguel Layún]] lashed his effort over from close range. South Korea wanted a penalty of their own after the restart when [[Moon Seon-min]]'s strike clipped [[Carlos Salcedo]]'s arm, but the referee waved away their appeals. Jo lunged to his right to tip [[Javier Hernández]]'s shot wide.<ref name="Goal South Korea v Mexico">{{cite web |last=Ridge |first=Patric |title=Hernandez nets landmark goal as last 16 beckons |url=http://www.goal.com/en/match/korea-republic-v-mexico/9jxgq4wwe6nxt5vuukii7vsh5 |website=Goal.com |date=23 June 2018}}</ref> Lozano drove into space, Vela drew away to the right as the ball went left to Hernández, who checked back and clipped low past Jo.<ref name="BBC South Korea v Mexico">{{cite web |last=Skelton |first=Jack |title=South Korea 1 Mexico 2 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44439169 |work=BBC Sport |date=23 June 2018}}</ref> In the third minute of stoppage time, Son struck from 20-yards into the top-left corner.<ref name="Goal South Korea v Mexico"/>

Before Son's goal, South Korea had gone 288 minutes without scoring at the World Cup, their longest ever such drought.<ref name="KOR-MEX recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/mexico-momentum-continues-korea-republic-left-reeling-2966451 |title=Mexico momentum continues, Korea Republic left reeling |publisher=FIFA |date=23 June 2018 |access-date=23 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520050517/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/mexico-momentum-continues-korea-republic-left-reeling-2966451 |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref> Hernández scored his 50th goal for Mexico, becoming the inaugural player of the Mexico national team to reach that milestone. Mexico has won consecutive matches at the World Cup starting with their inaugural achievement at the 2002 World Cup. Hernández is the third player to score at three World Cups, preceded by Mexico's [[Cuauhtémoc Blanco]] and [[Rafael Márquez]].<ref name="BBC South Korea v Mexico"/>

